{
  "name": "Find new Swiss companies from the Zefix and SHAB register as qualified B2B leads",
  "active": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nThis workflow helps Swiss agencies, accountants, insurers and B2B sales teams reach new companies in their first days. Every weekday it fetches new commercial register entries (SHAB rubric HR01, the same data as Zefix) for your cantons through an Apify actor. It keeps the legal forms you want, applies your include and exclude keywords to the name and company purpose, and skips every company already in your Google Sheet. New companies are added to the sheet and you get one email summary. Days without a match send nothing. A failed Apify run sends an alert.\n\n### Setup\nYou need an Apify account (the free plan works, the actor charges per record), Google Sheets and Gmail.\n1. Create a Header Auth credential: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`.\n2. Create a sheet with a tab named `Leads` and these columns in row 1: uid, name, legal_form, seat, canton, address, purpose, matched_keywords, published, shab_url.\n3. Fill in the Configuration node: cantons, sheet URL, tab name, your email.\n4. Connect Google Sheets and Gmail, run once and check the sheet.\n\n### Customization\nLegal form codes: 0106 AG, 0107 GmbH, 0101 sole proprietorship. Leave includeKeywords empty to keep all companies. Publication takes a few days after founding, so lookbackDays covers weekends.",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "fe4c00f0-78c4-5218-be94-77241470663c",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -600,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Fetch new registrations\nLoads the settings and asks Apify for fresh HR01 notices from the Swiss Official Gazette of Commerce.",
        "height": 300,
